          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>

        <!-- =============================================================
             ANNOTATION explaining T1 / DMA cooperation
             ============================================================= -->
        <mxCell id="note_coop" parent="1" vertex="1"
          value="How T1 and DMA cooperate&#10;&#10;The vector core does not talk to the DMA engine directly. Instead, both connect to the&#10;Compute Data Crossbar, which gives them coordinated access to the same on-chip&#10;scratchpad. Typical use: software programs the DMA to copy a tile of pixels from&#10;DDR &#8594; scratchpad, then kicks off the T1 to process that tile in place, then DMA copies&#10;the result back to DDR. The scratchpad acts as a high-bandwidth handoff buffer."
          style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFDE7;strokeColor=#827717;strokeWidth=1;dashed=1;fontSize=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=8;fontColor=#212121;">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="730" width="240" height="200" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

